      "writtenOn": "2026-09-15T16:32:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The `contains(T item)` was created for the sole purpose of using `DynamicSet\u003c\u003e` here as a surrogate of a set, see https://gerrit-review.googlesource.com/c/gerrit/+/70072/8/gerrit-extension-api/src/main/java/com/google/gerrit/extensions/registration/DynamicSet.java.\n\nThe implementation of `contains()` is quite expensive because it performs a full scan of all items in the `DynamicSet\u003c\u003e`, looking for the *same item* rather than the *equal object*.\n\nI am indeed changing the implementation here, I agree, compared to the original version. However, I could argue that the original implementation was not optimised, as we execute this check for *every request* that passes through the Gerrit HTTP pipeline.\n\nI can keep the semantics here by introducing a method that performs a full scan as it did before, and then remove it in the follow-up. If anyone complains about two plugins having the same AllRequestFilter active at the same time, then we can revisit the choice and just remove the optimisation.\n\nWhat do you think?",
