      "side": 1,
      "message": "The `init()` at L149 runs once when Jetty starts and initialises only the `filters` in the `DynamicSet`.\n\nLater, when a plugin is loaded, Gerrit attaches that plugin\u0027s filter to the same `filters` DynamicSet, but this `FilterProxy.init()` is not called again.\n\nThat\u0027s why those plugin filters are initialised lazily on their first HTTP request:\n\n```\nif (initializedFilters.contains(filter) || initFilterIfNeeded(filter)) {\n  filter.doFilter(...);\n}\n```\n\nIf one filter has never passed through this initialisation (because it received no requests), we will `destroy` a filter that was never initialised (in the previous implementation we were only looping through _initialised_ filters).\n\n\n\nCalling `destroy()` can then fail with an `NPE`, for example:\n\n\n```\nclass XXXAuditFilter extends AllRequestFilter {\n  private AuditClient client;\n\n  @Override\n  public void init(FilterConfig config) {\n    client \u003d new AuditClient(config);\n  }\n\n  @Override\n  public void destroy() {\n    client.close();\n  }\n}\n```\n\nCould `destroy()` keep iterating over the initialised filters instead?",
